From fda07fbbacb98a689d5dbe857ab894095a8f51c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 03:49:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: mediatek: propagate advanced pull resistor errors

The advanced-pull setter returns success when either the R0 or R1 field
write fails. A missing resistor field can therefore accept a request
without configuring the requested pull. An R1 failure can also leave
the already-written R0 field changed while reporting success.

Return the field error to the pinconf caller. Preserve the successful
sequence and the existing PUPD fallback; do not attempt rollback of an
earlier field write.

Unsigned experiment draft; archive identity is non-certifying.
---
 drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mtk-common-v2.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mtk-common-v2.c b/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mtk-common-v2.c
index faa6dbf..7351dc6 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mtk-common-v2.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mtk-common-v2.c
@@ -1151,12 +1151,12 @@ int mtk_pinconf_adv_pull_set(struct mtk_pinctrl *hw,
 	 */
 	err = mtk_hw_set_value(hw, desc, PINCTRL_PIN_REG_R0, arg & 1);
 	if (err)
-		return 0;
+		return err;
 
 	err = mtk_hw_set_value(hw, desc, PINCTRL_PIN_REG_R1,
 			       !!(arg & 2));
 	if (err)
-		return 0;
+		return err;
 
 	arg = pullup ? 0 : 1;
 
-- 
